## 4. How these use cases were chosen

Every process step was rated against a rubric drawn from public frameworks: the money lever it touches, error cost and type of knowledge (HBR), whether the task is repetitive, a bottleneck, or ambiguous (OpenAI, Taylor Radey), the full cost including human review (MIT Sloan), and feasibility in data, systems, and know-how (appliedAI). The most promising steps were matched against a library of AI use cases already running elsewhere, and three were adapted to this company.

